  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Sky Outside, Night Inside",
    "overview": "The sky is a picture and the rooms are dark and neutral. A blue sky gradient covers the sign-in ground and shows up as generated imagery (server avatars, placeholders, title cards). Every surface you work on is near-black, cool-neutral and untinted. One electric blue does the pointing (focus rings, the active page dot, links, switches), and the only bright fill is the white pill primary action. Layout and journey mirror the Android client (Jujo.StreamClient): sign-in sheet, focus-mode server carousel, Hero launcher with a poster row, then the stream.\n\nThe density is calm, at phone scale. The minimum sizes are text 13px, inputs 16px and touch targets 44px. Hover behaves exactly like focus on fine pointers. Motion is short and uses a single curve. Decorative loops run only where the user is not working (the sign-in sky, the focused server's float and the background ribbons). They stop before the stream starts, because the stream needs the GPU.",
